          "text": "Description: On January 24, 1976, several people, including gendarmes, observed a distant, glowing object in the sky between 7:40 PM and 10:30 PM, emitting green and orange lights. The object moved significantly. No noise was heard. All these witnesses likely made an astronomical observation of the star Sirius, which is particularly well-visible during this time of year.",
